# PRESSURE COOKER ARTICHOKES
## info  
* About 5 minutes prep, 30 minutes total
* 2 servings  

## ingredients
* 2 medium artichokes
* 1 cup water
* 1 lemon, quartered
* 2 cloves garlic
* 2 tablespoons butter
* 2 tablespoons olive oil
* pinch black pepper
* pinch salt

## steps  
1. Place the rack insert or steamer insert into the bowl of your electric pressure cooker so that the artichokes can sit above the water. 
1. Add water to the machine and then the artichokes on top of the rack in a single layer. It doesn't matter if they are stem side up or down. 
1. Toss two quarters of squeezed lemon into the pressure cooker if desired.
1. Lock the lid to seal. Set to cook on high for 15 minutes. When finished, quick release the pressure.
1. While artichokes are cooking, melt butter and oil in an 8 inch skillet. Add garlic, salt, pepper and cook 1 minute. Remove from heat and add strained juice from remaining lemon. Add to ramekins or small dishes for dipping.

